-- title:
--   Gauss-valuation anchor transported from the cyclotomic witness
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a natural number $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$.
--
--   **Coefficient field and roots of unity.** $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity with $\zeta = \xi^{\ell}$, and the hypothesis `hι` asserts that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$.
--
--   **Level group and function field.** $H_1$ is the subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ equal to the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$ (the latter through $\ell \mid q^2 M'$); thus $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. $K$ is the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ given by [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the Fourier-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionFieldC ℚ (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L76) of level $\Gamma_{H_1}$.
--
--   **Base ring and point.** $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q$ in the maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_A$, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$, and with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$; $j \in K$ is the element whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ is the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the Fourier expansion of the modular $j$-invariant, and $j \neq 0$; $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak{m}_A$; and $t \in A$ satisfies $t^{q-1} = q w$ for some unit $w$. Further, $z$ is a point of the scheme [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the two chart algebras (the elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, respectively over $A[j^{-1}]$) along their common middle chart; $\varpi z$ is the germ at $z$ of the global section obtained from $\varpi$ through `toBase`, and `hz` asserts that it lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$; $y$ is a point of $\mathrm{XFin} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-finite chart algebra with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y) = z$; and the hypothesis `hss` asserts that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the $j$-finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is, every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The cyclotomic witness.** All of the preceding geometric data is duplicated over a field $L_0$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of conductor $q\ell$: roots of unity $\zeta_0, \xi_0$ with $\zeta_0 = \xi_0^{\ell}$, the same function field $K_0 =$ `laurentBaseChange L₀ (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`, a discrete valuation domain $A_0$ with fraction field $L_0$ containing $q$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta_0$ in its image, an $A_0$-algebra structure on $K_0$, the element $j_0 \neq 0$ with Fourier expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), a uniformiser $\varpi_0$, a point $z_0$ of `TwoChartIntegralModel A₀ K₀ j₀` with $\varpi_0$-germ $\varpi z_0$ in the maximal ideal of the stalk, a point $y_0$ of the $j$-finite chart with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y_0) = z_0$, and the supersingularity hypothesis `hss₀` in the same form as `hss`. No hypothesis on the residue field of $A_0$ is made.
--
--   **Comparison data.** A ring homomorphism $i : L_0 \to L$ with $i(\zeta_0) = \zeta$ and $i(\xi_0) = \xi$; an $A_0$-algebra structure on $A$ whose structure map is a local homomorphism and injective and is compatible with $i$ through the fraction fields (`hA₀A`); the image of $\varpi_0$ in $A$ equals $t$ times a unit; a ring homomorphism $c_K : K_0 \to K$ acting coefficientwise by [`ModularCurve.coeffMap i`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L16) on Laurent expansions, with $c_K(j_0) = j$; a ring homomorphism $c$ between the $j$-finite chart algebras compatible with $c_K$, with $\mathrm{comap}\, c\, (y) = y_0$; and a ring isomorphism $\beta : A \otimes_{A_0} (\text{chart algebra over } A_0) \to (\text{chart algebra over } A)$ with $\beta(a \otimes b) = a \cdot c(b)$.
--
--   **Formal local charts.** $W_0$ is a discrete valuation domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal, with a ring homomorphism $\sigma_0 : A_0 \to W_0$ such that $\mathfrak{m}_{W_0} = (\sigma_0\varpi_0)$; $f_0, u_0, v_0 \in W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_0, v_0$ units and $f_0 \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ ([`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)); and $e_0$ is a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of the stalk at $z_0$ onto $S_0 := W_0[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_0\varpi_0)v_0 - f_0u_0)$. On the $A$-side, $\psi : W_0 \to \widehat{A}$ (the $\mathfrak{m}_A$-adic completion) satisfies $\psi \circ \sigma_0 =$ the composite $A_0 \to A \to \widehat{A}$; $f, u, v \in \widehat{A}[[X_0,X_1]]$ are given with no unit hypotheses on $u, v$; $e$ is a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := \widehat{A}[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\hat t)v - fu)$, where $\hat t$ is the image of $t$ in $\widehat{A}$; and `hrel` asserts that the image of $C(\sigma_0\varpi_0)v_0 - f_0u_0$ under $\psi$ applied coefficientwise lies in the ideal generated by $C(\hat t)v - fu$.
--
--   Write $\mathrm{toC}$ for the canonical map from a stalk into its adic completion, $\mathrm{mkS}$ (respectively $\mathrm{mkS}_0$) for the quotient map onto $S$ (respectively $S_0$), and $\mathrm{germY}$ (respectively $\mathrm{germY}_0$) for the homomorphism from the $j$-finite chart algebra into the stalk at $z$ (respectively $z_0$) obtained by composing the inverse of the global-sections isomorphism for $\operatorname{Spec}$, the inverse of the isomorphism of $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ on $\top$, and the germ map at the point over the open image of $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$.
--
--   **Anchor over the witness (`hanchor₀`).** For every prime ideal $P$ of $S_0$ with $\mathrm{mkS}_0(X_0) \notin P$ or $\mathrm{mkS}_0(X_1) \notin P$, with $\mathrm{mkS}_0(C(\sigma_0\varpi_0)) \in P$, and such that $\mathrm{mkS}_0\big(C(1)X_0 + C(0)X_1 + h\big) \in P$ for some $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and for every $a$ in the $j$-finite chart algebra over $A_0$: $\mathrm{toC}_0(\mathrm{germY}_0(a))$ lies in the preimage of $P$ under $e_0$ if and only if for every $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ the $n$-th Laurent coefficient of $a$, viewed in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L_0)$, is the image of an element of $\mathfrak{m}_{A_0}$.
--
--   **Constants (`hconst`).** For every $a \in A$, $e$ carries the image in the completion of the germ at $z$ of the global section attached to $a$ through `toBase` to $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\hat a))$.
--
--   **Compatibility (`hcompat`).** For every $x$ in the chart algebra over $A_0$ and every $s \in W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$: if $e_0$ carries the image in the completion of $\mathrm{germY}_0(x)$ to the class of $s$, then $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(c(x)))) = \mathrm{mkS}(\psi_*(s))$, where $\psi_*$ is $\psi$ applied coefficientwise.
--
--   **Noetherianity (`hnoeth`).** The $j$-finite chart algebra over $A$ is a Noetherian ring.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every prime ideal $P$ of $S$ such that
--
--   (i) $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0) \notin P$ or $\mathrm{mkS}(X_1) \notin P$;
--
--   (ii) $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\hat\varpi)) \in P$, where $\hat\varpi$ is the image of $\varpi$ in $\widehat{A}$;
--
--   (iii) there is $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2 \subseteq \widehat{A}[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $\mathrm{mkS}\big(C(1)X_0 + C(0)X_1 + h\big) \in P$;
--
--   (iv) there is $h_0 \in (X_0,X_1)^2 \subseteq W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $\mathrm{mkS}\big(\psi_*(C(1)X_0 + C(0)X_1 + h_0)\big) \in P$
--
--   (the combinations in (iii) and (iv) being $X_0 + h$ and $\psi_*(X_0 + h_0)$), the following holds for every $a$ in the $j$-finite chart algebra over $A$: $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ lies in the preimage of $P$ under $e$ if and only if for every $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ there is $m \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ with $n$-th Laurent coefficient of $a$, viewed in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$, equal to the image of $m$ in $L$.
--
--   Thus the preimage in the chart algebra of such a branch prime is exactly the prime of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients are in $\mathfrak{m}_A$, the identification over $A$ being deduced from the corresponding identification over $A_0$.
--
--   This is the base-change step of the identification of the branch primes on the Drinfeld local chart at a supersingular point of the integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}$ with the Gauss prime given by coefficientwise divisibility by the uniformiser: the identification is assumed over the cyclotomic witness $(L_0, A_0)$ and is transported along the comparison data to $(L, A)$ with algebraically closed residue field. It feeds the construction of the isomorphism of the completed stalk with the Drinfeld chart quotient in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_baseChange_of_cyclotomicWitness_of_isAlgClosed_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_baseChange_of_cyclotomicWitness_of_isAlgClosed_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd).
